====================================================
PhantomRing (agent) - Static Analysis Notes
====================================================

APPROACH
--------
Binary was not stripped, so symbol names were visible.
Method: strings -> symbol names -> disassembly around
key calls -> raw .rodata bytes to confirm exact strings.


STEP-BY-STEP METHOD
--------------------

1. Identify file type
   $ file agent
   -> ELF 64-bit PIE, dynamically linked, not stripped

2. Hash the sample
   $ sha256sum agent

3. Grep strings for quick wins (IP, keywords)
   $ strings agent | grep -E "([0-9]{1,3}\.){3}[0-9]{1,3}"
   $ strings agent | grep -iE "port|connect|sleep|reconnect"
   -> found C2 IP and io_uring_prep_connect symbol

4. Disassemble around connect logic for the port
   $ objdump -d agent | grep -B10 "io_uring_prep_connect"
   -> mov $0x115d,%edi ; call htons@plt
   -> 0x115d = 4445 decimal

5. Find reconnect delay
   $ objdump -d agent | grep -B10 "call.*sleep@plt"
   -> mov $0x78,%edi -> 120 seconds

6. Enumerate command handlers
   $ strings agent | grep -B3 -A3 "cmd_"
   $ objdump -d agent | grep -A20 "<main>"
   -> 11 handler symbols found directly

7. Trace each handler for target paths/strings
   $ objdump -d agent | grep -A30 "<cmd_users>"
     -> /var/run/utmp
   $ objdump -d agent | grep -A40 "<cmd_killbpf>"
   $ strings agent | grep -iE "bpf|\.so|maps"
     -> /proc/%s/maps , anon_inode:bpf-map
   $ strings agent | grep -iE "tracing|ftrace|debugfs"
     -> tracing_on, set_event, current_tracer
   $ strings agent | grep "/proc"
     -> /proc/self/exe

8. Confirm exact self-destruct command string from raw bytes
   $ objdump -d agent | grep -B15 "call.*cmd_selfdestruct"
     (find .rodata offset used in strcmp)
   $ objdump -s -j .rodata agent | grep -A1 "54c0|54c8|54d0"
     (dump that exact offset)
   -> ASCII decode confirmed: sdestruct


