KEY TECHNIQUE TO REMEMBER
---------------------------
When strings/plain grep misses something (e.g. port or exact
wire-command string), fall back to:
  1. Disassemble around the relevant call instruction
  2. Note the RIP-relative offset comment (# 54cc <...>)
  3. Dump that exact offset from .rodata with:
     objdump -s -j .rodata agent
  4. Read the ASCII column directly - don't trust strings'
     line-splitting near string boundaries
